# Python Conventions

Apply when editing `src/**/*.py`. Read [doc/stack.md](../../doc/stack.md). Subagent: `build-agent`.

## Layout

Follow `layout` in `doc/stack.md` (typically `src/<package>/`).

## Style

- Prefer small functions, single responsibility
- Type hints on public APIs when the project uses them
- Match existing logging and error-handling patterns

## Naming

Full rules: [doc/coding-conventions.md](../../doc/coding-conventions.md). Follow PEP 8.

| Target | Case | Example |
|--------|------|---------|
| Variables, functions, methods | snake_case | `user_name`, `fetch_order` |
| Classes | PascalCase | `UserService` |
| Constants | SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE | `MAX_RETRY_COUNT` |
| Modules, packages | snake_case | `user_service.py` |
| Private | leading `_` | `_internal_state` |

Semantics: verb-first functions; `is`/`has`/`can` booleans; plural collections; English identifiers; comments may be Japanese.

## Before finishing

Use `test_all`, `typecheck`, `lint` from `doc/stack.md`.
